      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the average number of rounds of golf played by each golfer, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Sum the total number of rounds played by all golfers.**\n2. **Count the total number of golfers.**\n3. **Divide the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers to find the average.**\n\nFrom the chart, we have the following number of rounds played by each golfer:\n- 1 golfer played 5 rounds.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 3 golfers played 3 rounds each.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds each.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\n\\[\n5 \\text{ rounds} + 2 \\times 2 \\text{ rounds} + 2 \\times 2 \\text{ rounds} + 3 \\times 3 \\text{ rounds} + 5 \\times 5 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 1 = 5 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\times 3 = 9 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 5 = 25 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n5 + 4 + 4 + 9 + 25 = 47 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we count the total number of golfers. From the chart, the total number of golfers is:\n\n\\[\n1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 13\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the average number of rounds played by each golfer by dividing the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{47 \\text{ rounds}}{13 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 3.615\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
